Checking review comments for PR #42...

============================================================
  Review Comments Require Attention
============================================================

UNREPLIED COMMENTS (1):

  - src/a.ts:12 by @muhammed
    "please rename this..."

------------------------------------------------------------
Please address all review comments with SUBSTANTIVE replies.

Low-effort replies like 'Acknowledged', 'OK', 'Done', 'Fixed'
etc. are NOT accepted. Explain what you did or why you
disagree with the feedback.

Examples of good replies:
  - 'Fixed by adding null check in validateInput()'
  - 'Refactored to use the existing helper as suggested'
  - 'Keeping as-is because X needs to happen before Y due to...'

To reply using gh CLI:

  # List unreplied comments (find the COMMENT_ID you need to reply to)
  gh api repos/rediacc/console/pulls/42/comments \
    --jq '.[] | select(.in_reply_to_id == null) | {id, path, line, body}'

  # Reply to a specific comment (NOTE: PR number is required in the path!)
  gh api repos/rediacc/console/pulls/42/comments/{COMMENT_ID}/replies \
    -X POST -f body="Your substantive reply here"

  # IMPORTANT: The endpoint is /pulls/{PR_NUMBER}/comments/{COMMENT_ID}/replies
  # NOT /pulls/comments/{COMMENT_ID}/replies (this will return 404)

Or reply directly on GitHub:
  https://github.com/rediacc/console/pull/42
------------------------------------------------------------

UNANSWERED REVIEW SUMMARY (1):

  - comment 5189236393 by @github-actions[bot], posted 2026-08-05T10:00:00Z
    https://github.com/rediacc/console/pull/42#issuecomment-5189236393
    "x ```json:review-findings [] ..."

------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS BLOCKS. The automated review posts its verdict, its
severity-ordered defects, its nits and its coverage map as ONE
top-level comment. Only the top findings are mirrored inline
(capped at 20, and any whose line is not in the diff is dropped),
so resolving the inline threads does NOT address the summary.
Top-level comments have no thread and nothing to resolve, so the
only evidence anyone read it is a later comment answering it.
There is none.

WHAT A SUBSTANTIVE REPLY MUST CONTAIN. Go finding by finding, in
the summary's own order, and for each one state exactly one of:
  - fixed: what changed and in which commit
  - deferred: where it is tracked (issue or worklist id) and why
  - disagreed: the reason, concretely, not 'out of scope'
Answer the nits and the coverage map too: if the summary says an
area went unreviewed, say whether that is acceptable and why.
It must be posted by someone other than @github-actions[bot] (a
second comment from the reviewer is not an answer to the first),
and it must either cite 5189236393 or run past 200 characters.

To answer using gh CLI:

  # 1. Read the full summary first - the excerpt above is 120 chars
  gh api repos/rediacc/console/issues/comments/5189236393 --jq .body

  # 2. Post the answer as a NEW top-level comment
  gh api repos/rediacc/console/issues/42/comments -X POST \
    -f body="Re: review summary 5189236393

  - <finding 1 title>: fixed in <sha> - <what changed>
  - <finding 2 title>: not changing - <why>
  - <nit>: deferred to <issue/worklist id>

  Coverage: <the areas the summary flagged as unreviewed, and your call on them>"

  # IMPORTANT: a top-level comment has NO replies endpoint. All three
  # of these are wrong, and the first two return 404 (verified):
  #   repos/rediacc/console/issues/42/comments/5189236393/replies   -> 404
  #   repos/rediacc/console/pulls/42/comments/5189236393/replies    -> 404
  #     (that path is real, but only for INLINE comment ids;
  #      5189236393 is an ISSUE comment id and is not found there)
  #   repos/rediacc/console/issues/comments/5189236393  -> GET/PATCH only. That
  #     is the EDIT endpoint for the summary itself; posting there would
  #     overwrite the review, not answer it.

Or comment directly on GitHub:
  https://github.com/rediacc/console/pull/42#issuecomment-5189236393
